kidesktop Debian packaging
==========================

Three binary packages from one build of the top-level Makefile:

    kidesktop-core   the desktop (session, WM, compositor, panel, settings...)
    kidesktop-base   the applications (kiterm, kifiles, ...)
    kidesktop        empty metapackage depending on both

`make install-core` / `make install-base` fill each package's directory.

debian/changelog is not kept in git: scripts/build-deb.sh writes it for
each build, with the version taken from the git tag (v1.2.3 -> 1.2.3, or
0.0.0+git<date>.<commit> between tags) plus a distro suffix
(~ubuntu22.04, ~debian12) so the per-distro builds of one release can
sit side by side in a release's assets.

    make deb            # -> dist/kidesktop-core_*.deb, kidesktop-base_*.deb,
                        #    kidesktop_*_all.deb
